bw-port: the stuck-input checks (docs/perf.md "Stuck buttons"), cheap enough to stay on in the maintainer's builds. Lines only when
something is off: "anomaly: WHAT, tick T" (20 a minute) and, on iOS, "stall: tick T: N ms (parts...)" for a frame over 50 ms.
sim_touch.cpp: a finger UIKit ended or cancelled whose end did not reach the touch layer in that dispatch is let go at once
(SimTouch_UIKitEnded, from port/src/ios_input.m); once a frame every held finger is checked against UIKit's record (ended
100 ms ago: let go; missing from UIKit's touch events: logged); a down for a finger still held lets the old one go; UIKit's
cancels on SDL's view are logged; the "input: release N ms late" line names the buttons and the tick (30 a minute).
sim_main.cpp: SIM_Anomaly / SIM_PadNames / SIM_InputTickNo; the keyboard's (iOS) and the game controller's held masks against
the devices' state (150 ms stale: let go); a controller disconnect while holding is logged; the frame stamps always taken.
Windows/Linux: 8 clock reads a frame more, the stall line only with BWPORT_STALLLOG=1, the controller check only on the SDL game
controller path (BWPORT_PAD_GC), a disconnect line; nothing else changes there.

